clk: tegra: gbus prepare sets the GPU rail's voltage, as in R32

R35 returns -ENOTSUPP from the gbus clock's prepare on kernels from 4.15
("FIXME Drop this check once dvfs feature is added to K59"). With the hang
gone (0007), the GPU's clock prepare would fail there and the power-on stop
with an error.

Do what R32.7.6's copy of this file does: set the GPU rail's voltage for the
current gbus rate with tegra_dvfs_set_rate(), which R35's built-in Tegra210
DVFS provides. 0022 does the same for the video engines' buses.

Tested on the Nano: with 0007, the GPU powered on in trial 8.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/nvidia/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-cbus-shared.c b/nvidia/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-cbus-shared.c
index bd86b5c3b..5aa31c541 100644
--- a/nvidia/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-cbus-shared.c
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-cbus-shared.c
@@ -11,9 +11,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 15, 0)
 #include <soc/tegra/tegra-dvfs.h>
-#endif
 
 #include "clk.h"
 
@@ -563,12 +561,14 @@ static unsigned long clk_shared_recalc_rate(struct clk_hw *hw,
 
 static int clk_gbus_prepare(struct clk_hw *hw)
 {
-	/* FIXME Drop this check once dvfs feature is added to K59 */
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 15, 0)
+	/*
+	 * R35 stubs this out (-ENOTSUPP) for kernels from 4.15, which makes
+	 * every prepare of a gbus user fail, nvgpu's gm20b power-on included.
+	 * Tegra210 DVFS is built on 5.10 (tegra-dvfs.c, tegra210-dvfs.c), so
+	 * raise the GPU rail for the current gbus rate before the GPU clock
+	 * runs, as R32 does.
+	 */
 	return tegra_dvfs_set_rate(hw->clk, clk_get_rate(hw->clk));
-#else
-	return -ENOTSUPP;
-#endif
 }
 
 static void clk_gbus_unprepare(struct clk_hw *hw)
